0,Southern Pomo Project – WIELD: Western Institute for Endangered...,https://wieldoc.org/?page_id=30,"Southern Pomo Project. FLV_Ps For a more detailed description of our fragmented languages scale, click here. Southern Pomo is one of seven mutually unintelligible Pomoan languages which are native to the Clear Lake and Russian River areas of Northern California.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
1,Pomoan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/3686/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..fzpaQBOHYudOhzPV0W9SpELwsjo4JpruGJEhMeWJESM,"Pomoan. Subgroup of 7 languages.Western 4. Pomo, Northern pej, a language of United States. Southern 3.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
2,"Pomo Language and the Pomo Indian Tribe (Pomoan, Kulanapan...)",https://www.native-languages.org/pomo.htm,Eastern Pomo Southern Pomo Northern Pomo: Encyclopedia articles on the Pomo Indian languages. Lenguas Pomoan Lenguas Pomoanas Pomo Langue: Pomo information in Spanish and French.,"Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
3,Southern Pomo | California Language Archive,https://cla.berkeley.edu/languages/southern-pomo.html,"The traditional Southern Pomo language area is on the lower Russian River, in the Dry Creek Valley, and on the Santa Rosa plain. In pre-contact times, the Pomoan languages together probably had around 8,000 speakers (Kroeber 1925).","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
4,Pomo Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Pomo,"They include Northern Pomo, Northeastern Pomo, Eastern Pomo, Southeastern Pomo, Central Pomo, Southern Pomo, and Kashaya. After European-American settlement, the Pomoan languages became seriously endangered.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
5,ERIC - ED553274 - A Grammar of Southern Pomo: An Indigenous...,https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED553274,"Southern Pomo is a moribund indigenous language, one of seven closely related Pomoan languages once spoken in Northern California in the vicinity of the Russian River drainage, Clear Lake, and the adjacent Pacific coast. This work is the first full-length grammar of the language.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
6,OLAC resources in and about the Southern Pomo language,http://olac.ldc.upenn.edu/language/peq,"ONLINEConversation about the Southern Pomo and their customs.ONLINE[Southern Pomo field notes]. Oswalt, Robert L. (researcher); Allen, Elsie (consultant); Oswalt family. [1986 November 6-16]. California Language Archive. oai:cla.berkeley.edu:Oswalt.001.006.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
7,loc.gov/item/mss326980246,https://www.loc.gov/item/mss326980246/,C. Hart Merriam Papers: Indian vocabularies; Pomoan; We'-shah' chum'-mi...,"Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
8,Language Revitalization – Dry Creek Rancheria,https://drycreekrancheria.com/language-revitalization/,"The Southern Pomo language, which lost its last fluent speaker in 2014. Southern Pomo is one of seven Pomoan languages once spoken in the vicinity of Clear Lake and the Russian River drainage of California.","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
9,Sprouting Valley,https://ethnobiology.org/sites/default/files/publications/contributions/Sprouting-Valley-2013-online.pdf,"Music: Hudson described the Potter Valley Pomo use of musical mouth bows made from light woods, such as dogwood, although Loeb later reported that these were only known among the Pomoan groups at Clear Lake (Loeb 1926).","Pomo, Southern",Pomoan
